{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["Q1", "Q3", "J5"],
      "pins": ["Q1.3", "Q3.gate/drain", "J5.2"],
      "nets": ["Q_PMC_GSD", "VCC_OUT"],
      "observed": "On the root sheet the fan power output net VCC_OUT (J5 pin 2) is joined at the same node to the gate-control net labelled Q_PMC_GSD and to Q1 (BC817) collector and one Q3 (PMOS) terminal. The Q3 gate terminal is instead tied to NET0009 (fan pin 4) and pulled to VCC by R7/JP2, so the PMOS gate is held at VCC (off) and the NPN Q1, driven by the PWM net NET0002, pulls VCC_OUT to GND.",
      "expected": "In a high-side PMOS fan switch the gate net (Q_PMC_GSD) must connect to the PMOS gate, the NPN collector and the pull-up (R7), while the PMOS drain/source must carry the switched supply VCC_OUT to the fan; the gate-control net must never be merged with the power output net.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "J5 FAN pin2 = VCC_OUT; node also labelled Q_PMC_GSD and tied to Q1 collector and Q3 terminal (root sheet)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "R7 10K and JP2 VCC_STABLE connect Q3 gate node NET0009 to VCC; Q1 base via R3 from NET0002"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "an ATtiny-driven fan controller"}
      ],
      "impact": "The fan never receives switched supply (PMOS gate stuck high) and the PWM line instead shorts VCC_OUT to ground through Q1; the fan is uncontrollable / does not run.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["J6"],
      "pins": ["J6.2", "J6.3"],
      "nets": ["NET0004", "NET0005"],
      "observed": "At the potentiometer J6 the wiper/bottom wire carries both the NET0004 label (the pot wiper / ADC node) and a NET0005 label, merging the analog speed-set net with the MCU RESET net (NET0005 = U1/U2 pin 1 RESET/PB5 and J3 pin 5 RST).",
      "expected": "The potentiometer wiper (NET0004) should be an isolated analog input; the RESET net (NET0005) must not be tied to the pot divider.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "J6 POT pin2 wire labelled NET0004 and NET0005 (root sheet)"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "NET0005 = U1.1/U2.1 RESET/PB5 and J3.5 RST (right sheet)"}
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU reset line is driven by the speed potentiometer, so the controller may be held in reset or reset unpredictably as the pot is turned.",
      "confidence": 0.35
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing shows the fan high-side switch miswired: the PMOS gate-control net Q_PMC_GSD is merged with the fan supply net VCC_OUT (and the NPN collector), leaving the fan unpowered and the PWM line shorting the output to ground; additionally the potentiometer node appears to bridge NET0004 with the RESET net NET0005."
}

